# 4. Current Content Structures

The current implemented content has two related but different module structures.

## Foundation

Foundation modules use frontmatter containing a `cabinetArtifact` object and a trailing portfolio section such as:

```text
Your First Portfolio Entry
Your Second Portfolio Entry
```

The exact numbering varies by module.

The validator must not require identical heading structures across all Foundation modules.

## OT Security

OT modules use a different structure, including a dedicated Cabinet section.

The known pattern is conceptually:

```text
Where you are
Section 1 scenario
Section 2 concept
Section 3 hands-on
Section 4 enterprise
Section 5 cabinet
What you can now do
```

Again, the validator must validate supported structural expectations rather than enforcing identical headings across module families.

