# 31. Acceptance Criteria

CP-AUTO-008 is complete when:

- [ ] Existing Cabinet definitions/types have been inspected and reused.
- [ ] Foundation and OT structures are handled separately where required.
- [ ] Deterministic Cabinet metadata checks are implemented.
- [ ] Artifact relationship checks are implemented where supported by repository data.
- [ ] Previous/next module references are validated.
- [ ] Self-reference is detected where prohibited.
- [ ] Unlock relationships are validated where a repository source of truth exists.
- [ ] Required hands-on structure is checked only where explicitly required.
- [ ] Required Cabinet/portfolio structure is checked only where explicitly required.
- [ ] Existing Foundation and OT modules are tested.
- [ ] Invalid fixtures cover representative failure cases.
- [ ] Findings conform to CP-AUTO-004.
- [ ] Cascading false positives are minimized.
- [ ] No AI is required.
- [ ] No content is automatically modified.
- [ ] No arbitrary commands or MDX code are executed.
- [ ] No new content or Cabinet schema is invented.

---

# 32. Definition of Done

CP-AUTO-008 is successful when CyberPivot can reliably answer the deterministic structural question:

> "Does this module's practical work and Cabinet artifact structure match the repository's defined content and progression model?"

It must leave these questions for later review:

> "Is this lab good?"

> "Is this artifact valuable?"

> "Is this learning progression pedagogically strong?"

Those are not deterministic QA questions.

